flash-linear-attention
----------------------
The Drama 3 backbone's chunked Gated DeltaNet prefill follows SGLang 0.5.21's chunk_gated_delta_rule
(Apache License 2.0). Its fla/ kernels are adapted from flash-linear-attention
(https://github.com/fla-org/flash-linear-attention), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023-2025, Songlin Yang, Yu Zhang.
The patches' zig/kernels/cuda/drama_gdn_chunk.cuh and zig/src/families/drama/backbone_gdn.zig mirror those
kernels; each kernel names the source kernel it follows. The MIT license text is in
LICENSES/MIT-flash-linear-attention.txt.

TensorFold
----------
The engine patches apply to TensorFold (https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0. scripts/build-engine.sh clones TensorFold at the commit pinned in engine/UPSTREAM
and applies the patches with `git am`.

The patches modify TensorFold files. They add Drama 3 support for the native CUDA engine: new source files under
zig/src/families/drama/, zig/src/server/ (the speech route, prompt and streaming), zig/src/native/drama_host.zig,
zig/kernels/cuda/drama_*.cu and zig/tests/cuda/drama_*.zig. They also change existing TensorFold files in
zig/build/, zig/src/core/, zig/src/cuda/, zig/src/native/ and zig/src/server/, plus CHANGELOG.md. Each patch's
commit message and diff state what it changes. The patches keep TensorFold's existing file headers and notices
unchanged.

TensorFold's own NOTICE file reads:

    TensorFold
    Copyright 2026 TensorFold contributors
    https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold

    TensorFold is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (LICENSE) from 0.6.0.
    Releases up to 0.5.0 were MIT-licensed, and code written before 0.6.0 keeps its
    MIT notice in LICENSES/MIT.txt. Third-party code and its licenses are listed in
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

TensorFold's LICENSES/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are in the checkout that scripts/build-engine.sh creates.

SGLang-Omni
-----------
The Drama 3 port follows the SGLang-Omni Drama 3 reference implementation
(https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang-omni, sglang_omni/models/fishaudio_drama3, revision ab095ef9), whose
files carry SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0. The qualification tools import the reference at run time to
compare outputs; this repository does not include its source files.

Fish Audio
----------
Built with Fish Audio.

The codec files listed above are a Derivative Work of the Fish Audio Materials. They reimplement, in Zig and
CUDA, Fish Speech's modded DAC: its quantizer decode (DownsampleResidualVectorQuantize.decode: RVQ codes, the
window-limited transformer and the ConvNeXt upsampler) and its causal decoder. They follow the geometry of
modded_dac.py and modded_dac_vq.yaml as vendored in SGLang-Omni. What changed from the original: the codec
decodes only, never encodes. Its weights are weight-norm folded and cast to FP16, and it decodes as SGLang-Omni's
FP16 ChannelsLastDecoder path does. codec_pth.zig reads codec.pth without Python.

This repository contains no Fish Audio model weights, no codec checkpoint and no Fish Speech source code. The
Drama 3 weights and codec are downloaded separately from Hugging Face (fishaudio/drama-3) under FACL v1.0.

